  jv r = {JVP_FLAGS_STRING, 0, 0, 0, {&s->refcnt}};
  return r;
}
```

`jvp_string_alloc(length)` allocates `sizeof(jvp_string) + length + 1` bytes. So `s->data` has `length + 1` bytes available. `memset(s->data, 0, length)` zeroes `length` bytes. The `+1` byte (the null terminator position at `s->data[length]`) is NOT zeroed.

